<item>
            <title>[LUDOC-559] Document how to build Lustre in Docker</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LUDOC-559</link>
                <project id="10070" key="LUDOC">Lustre Documentation</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Lustre can be built natively on a number of Linux operating systems.&lt;br/&gt;
It is further possible to build the lustre server and/or client in a docker container.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The aim of this LUDOC working item is the following (as discussed in the DWG meeting):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Document how to set up docker (to have a safe copy)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Documen how the lustre server and/or client can be build in docker&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Provide any docker files and/or script examples are required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The more this can be generalised, the better.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Bonus question (may warrant a separate item: how to run lustre in a container.)&lt;/p&gt;</description>
